{"surface": "event", "title": "Apple guides its March-quarter gross margin below 45% on January 28", "html": "<div class=\"ev ws\"><div class=\"evh\"><h2 class=\"title\">Apple guides its March-quarter gross margin below 45% on January 28</h2><p class=\"facts\"><span>The decision on Jan 28, 2027</span><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span class=\"src\">Known from Apple fiscal Q1 2027 earnings call and release</span></p><div class=\"hds\"><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"definition\"><summary>Definition</summary><div class=\"hdb text\"><p>At its fiscal first-quarter report, projected for January 28, 2027, Apple guides gross margin for the March quarter with a midpoint below 45.0%: a second step down after the 45%-46% it guided for the December quarter, against 47.9% reported for September.</p></div></details><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"notes\"><summary>Rationale</summary><div class=\"hdb\"><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:70\" data-note=\"note:70\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"Management warned &#x27;that memory costs could rise beyond the December quarter, while supply constraints may affect Mac and iPad into next year&#x27;, and September&#x27;s 47.9% carried about a point of tariff refunds that will not repeat. Against that, the March quarter leans more to Services, Apple raised iPhone prices by about $100, and it has &#x27;longer-term memory contracts&#x27;. A further step below 45% is somewhat less likely than holding the 45%-46% range: one chance in three.\"><p>Management warned &#x27;that memory costs could rise beyond the December quarter, while supply constraints may affect Mac and iPad into next year&#x27;, and September&#x27;s 47.9% carried about a point of tariff refunds that will not repeat. Against that, the March quarter leans more to Services, Apple raised iPhone prices by about $100, and it has &#x27;longer-term memory contracts&#x27;. A further step below 45% is somewhat less likely than holding the 45%-46% range: one chance in three.</p></div></div><h4 class=\"ev-k\">Evidence</h4><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:187\">benzinga.com</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:187:05b40289d11c\">The pressure point is the coming quarter. Apple expects a 45% to 46% gross margin, compared with 47.9% in the quarter just reported. Gross margin is the share of sales left after direct product and service costs, before other business expenses.</a></blockquote><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:187:ebc319f67df1\">Higher memory-chip and AI costs are part of the squeeze. The comparison also includes a benefit that will not necessarily repeat: tariff refunds lifted the reported quarter’s margin by about one percentage point.</a></blockquote></div><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:185\">benzinga.com</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:185:a4e2cb356e96\">At the same time, investors continue to weigh management’s warning that memory costs could rise beyond the December quarter, while supply constraints may affect Mac and iPad into next year.</a></blockquote></div></div></details></div></div><div class=\"strip\" data-count=\"5\" style=\"--cols:5\"><div class=\"sf first\" data-k=\"fig:Forecast\"><span class=\"lab\">Forecast</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:23\"><span class=\"n v\">33.0%</span></a></span><a class=\"cap go calc\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:23\">How it’s set →</a></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If Yes\"><span class=\"lab\">If Yes</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:23:yes\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$1,677</span></a></span><span class=\"cap\"><span class=\"n loss\">−0.33%</span> of portfolio</span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If No\"><span class=\"lab\">If No</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:23:no\"><span class=\"n v gain\">+$826</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Full impact\"><span class=\"lab\">Full impact</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:swing:prop:23\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$2,503</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Volatility\"><span class=\"lab\">Volatility</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:volatility:prop:23\"><span class=\"n v\">±$1,270</span></a></span></div></div><nav class=\"tabs\" role=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"outcomes\">Outcomes</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"probability\">Probability</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"assumptions\">Assumptions</button></nav><section data-pane=\"outcomes\"><div class=\"ev-card po-card\" data-k=\"payoff\"><div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"plab\">P&amp;L by outcome</span><div class=\"rank po-switch\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"When\"><button type=\"button\" data-payoff=\"now\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Today</button><button type=\"button\" data-payoff=\"dated\">On Jan 28</button></div></div><div class=\"po-pane\" data-payoff-pane=\"now\"><div class=\"po-row\" data-outcome=\"yes\"><div class=\"po-lab\"><span class=\"po-title\">Yes</span><span class=\"po-p n\">33.0%</span></div><div class=\"po-track\"><i class=\"po-zero\" style=\"left:49.461%\"></i><i class=\"po-seg loss\" style=\"left:6.897%;right:calc(100% - 49.461%)\"></i></div><div class=\"po-val\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:23:yes\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$1,677</span></a></div></div><div class=\"po-row\" data-outcome=\"prop:24\"><div class=\"po-lab\"><span class=\"po-title\">Apple guides March-quarter gross margin at 45% to 46%</span><span class=\"otag\">Baseline</span><span class=\"po-p n\">47.0%</span></div><div class=\"po-track\"><i class=\"po-zero\" style=\"left:49.461%\"></i><i class=\"po-seg gain\" style=\"left:49.461%;right:calc(100% - 60.776%)\"></i></div><div class=\"po-val\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:o